+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Requests a page of conversation summaries for the authenticated user. The user id is taken from the connection and never from the frame, so an extra `userId` field cannot select another user's history ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 20,
+  "before": {"updatedAt": "2026-10-27T10:00:00.000Z", "sessionId": "session-3"}
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Description |
+|-------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `type` | string | Yes | `"list_sessions"` |
+| `limit` | number | No | Non-negative integer page size |
+| `before` | object | No | Cursor with `updatedAt` (ISO string or epoch number) and `sessionId` |
+
 ## 5. Server-to-Client Messages
 
 ### 5.1 connected
@@ -357,6 +375,17 @@ Semantics:
 - The client SHOULD use this message to clear any "processing" or "loading" indicators.
 - The client MUST treat a run as complete only at `stream_end` or when the socket closes. Unparseable JSON is the one frame answered with `INVALID_FORMAT` and no `stream_end`, because the server cannot tell what it was meant to be; for it the client falls back on the socket closing.
 
+### 5.9 session_list
+
+Answers `list_sessions` with summaries for the authenticated user. A summary contains metadata only; timestamps are ISO-8601 strings on the wire ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|-------|------|-------------|
+| `type` | string | `"session_list"` |
+| `sessions` | array | Page of conversation summaries |
+
+Each summary has `sessionId` (string), `createdAt` (ISO-8601 string), `updatedAt` (ISO-8601 string), and `entryCount` (number). The server does not push `session_list` unsolicited. A store without `listFor` answers an empty `sessions` array; a store failure is answered with `SERVER_ERROR` ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L136)).
+
 ## 6. SessionEntry Objects
 
 A SessionEntry represents a single piece of content in the conversation. Every entry has a `role` field that determines its shape. The `role` acts as a discriminant for the union type.
